# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lain — .gitignore
#
# Design rule: every pattern below is narrow and named. Nothing here can hide
# source code, specifications, or project documentation. Where a category could
# plausibly collide with real content, the specific filename is listed instead
# of a wildcard directory.
#
# Created during the P0 preparation task. NOT staged and NOT committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Audit staging ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The 2026-11-05 architecture audit staged 142 files (~149 MB) here, including
# ~148 MB of SQLite benchmark databases. It is evidence, not project content,
# and is scheduled for relocation outside the repository. Ignoring it prevents
# a `git add -A` from committing 149 MB of throwaway data into project history.
# This is the single most likely way to damage the repository today.
.lain-audit/

# ── Local runtime state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent/session state is per-machine and per-run. AGENTS.md's session-init
# protocol reads some of this; none of it is shared or reviewable.
.lain/

# ── Databases (runtime data, regenerable) ────────────────────────────────────
# Lain's event log and knowledge store are local SQLite. WAL and shared-memory
# sidecars are produced at runtime and are never meaningful in a commit.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── Secrets and local environment ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Owner rule: no secrets in git. `.env.example` is explicitly re-included
# because it is the documented, secret-free template that lists required vars.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Model files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Weights are multi-gigabyte binaries owned by Ollama's store, not by this
# repository. These extensions are unambiguous — no source or doc uses them.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.onnx

# ── Generated output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build outputs only. Deliberately NOT ignoring `build/`, `out/`, `lib/`,
# or `bin/`: those names are ambiguous and a wildcard could hide real source.
dist/
target/
coverage/

# ── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Python (audit and tooling scripts) ───────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ── Logs and temporary files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
*~

# ── Editor and OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scoped to the directories themselves; if a shared editor config is ever
# wanted, add a negation for that exact path rather than removing the rule.
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
